    "function": "Has a dual function in both nitrogen assimilation and in protection against acid stress during infection through asparagine hydrolysis and NH4(+) release. Catalyzes asparagine hydrolysis. Cannot use glutamine. Required for intracellular survival inside macrophages during host colonization. Mediates phagosome acidification arrest and resistance to acid stress through the formation of acid-neutralizing NH4(+) ions. In addition, may induce stress to primary immune cells and compromise the host immune response",
